The '''Indian Ocean''' is the world's third-largest [[ocean]], at {{convert|73,400,000|sqkm}}. It is surrounded by [[Asia]] to the north, [[Australia]] and the [[Pacific Ocean]] to the east, the [[Southern Ocean]] to the south, and [[Africa]] and the [[Atlantic Ocean]] to the west. It is named for the [[Indian subcontinent]] which projects into it. The [[Bay of Bengal]], the [[Arabian Sea]], the [[Persian Gulf]], and the [[Red Sea]] are all parts of the ocean. 

The deepest point in the Indian Ocean is in the Java Trench, near the [[Sunda Islands]], in the east, at {{convert|7,500|m}}. The ocean's average depth is {{convert|3,890|m}}. The majority of the ocean is in the [[southern hemisphere]].         

