'''Cognitive science''' studies how people make their [[idea|ideas]] and what makes [[thought|thoughts]] [[logical]]. It is often seen as the result of several different scientific fields working together. These fields are [[psychology]] (a study of the mind), neuroscience (biological study of the brain), [[computer science]] (the creation of programs and computers), and [[linguistics]] (the study of language). It does not refer to the sum of all these disciplines. It refers to their intersection on specific problems.
